    'intro'  => '<p>Phoenix&rsquo;s short-term rental market is shaped by its climate. Mild, sunny winters draw seasonal residents from colder states, spring training baseball fills the Valley in February and March, and demand for furnished rentals typically peaks during those months. Summers are extremely hot, and that is often when renters with flexible dates find more choice.</p><p>The Phoenix area is a sprawling metro made up of several cities, including Tempe, Scottsdale, Mesa, and Chandler, and many people live in one city while working in another. Most residents drive, and the freeway network is extensive, so choosing a location near your job or campus helps. Tempe tends to suit students and young professionals, Scottsdale draws seasonal visitors and those who want resort amenities, and central Phoenix offers the most direct light rail access to downtown.</p><p>Short-term demand also comes from travel nurses at the large hospital systems, students at Arizona State University, and a steady stream of relocations. <strong>Ask about air conditioning and covered parking</strong>, which are essentials rather than extras in the summer.</p>',
