      ['name' => 'Arcadia', 'blurb' => 'Established neighborhood between Phoenix and Scottsdale, known for mature trees, larger homes, and views of Camelback Mountain.'],
      ['name' => 'Tempe', 'blurb' => 'A separate city home to Arizona State University\'s main campus, with a lively Mill Avenue district, light rail, and a streetcar.'],
      ['name' => 'Scottsdale', 'blurb' => 'A separate city known for resorts, golf, Old Town nightlife, and upscale shopping. Popular with seasonal renters.'],
      ['name' => 'Midtown Phoenix', 'blurb' => 'Central area along the light rail on Central Avenue, close to downtown and several hospitals.'],
    ],
    'prices' => '<p>Phoenix is generally more affordable than California cities, but prices rise noticeably during the winter high season. Furnished private rooms commonly advertise somewhere in the $700&ndash;$1,200 per month range, while entire furnished one-bedrooms in central Phoenix, Tempe, and Scottsdale typically run higher, often $1,500 or more.</p><p>These ranges are rough, not official data. Prices vary by season, neighborhood and furnishing, with winter and spring often the most expensive, so compare current listings before committing.</p>',
    'transit'=> '<p>Valley Metro operates a light rail line connecting Phoenix, Tempe, and Mesa, along with the Tempe Streetcar and a bus network. The PHX Sky Train links Phoenix Sky Harbor International Airport to the light rail. Even so, the Phoenix area is mostly car-dependent, and you will likely want a car unless you live and work along the light rail corridor.</p><p>Sky Harbor is close to downtown and is the main airport for the region.</p>',
    'tips' => [
      'interns'  => 'Many internships are in Downtown Phoenix, Tempe, and the Scottsdale and Chandler tech corridors. Summer internships coincide with the hottest months, so look for reliable air conditioning and covered parking.',
      'nurses'   => 'Major employers include Banner Health (including Banner - University Medical Center Phoenix), Mayo Clinic Arizona, HonorHealth, Phoenix Children\'s, Valleywise Health, and St. Joseph\'s Hospital and Medical Center. Winter contracts are popular, so book early for that season.',
      'students' => 'Arizona State University in Tempe is the main institution, with additional campuses in Downtown Phoenix and elsewhere in the Valley. Grand Canyon University is also in Phoenix. Summer sublets near ASU are common.',
      'seasonal' => 'Demand peaks in winter and spring, with seasonal residents and spring training in February and March. Summer is quieter because of the heat, which can mean better options and prices.',
    ],
    'faqs' => [
      ['q' => 'When is peak season for furnished rentals in Phoenix?', 'a' => 'Winter and spring, roughly from late fall through March or April, when seasonal visitors and spring training increase demand. Summer is usually quieter.'],
      ['q' => 'Do I need a car in Phoenix?', 'a' => 'Most residents rely on one. If you live and work along the light rail between Phoenix, Tempe, and Mesa, you may be able to get by without a car.'],
      ['q' => 'What should I check before renting in Phoenix in summer?', 'a' => 'Make sure the air conditioning works well, ask about typical electric bills, and look for covered or garage parking to protect your car from the sun.'],
    ],
  ],

