    'type'   => 'metro',
    'lat'    => 40.4406, 'lng' => -79.9959,
    'tagline'=> 'Affordable furnished sublets for UPMC rotations, CMU and Pitt terms, and tech internships, across Pittsburgh\'s hilly river neighborhoods.',
    'intro'  => '<p>Pittsburgh has reinvented itself around healthcare, universities, and technology, and its short-term housing market reflects that shift. UPMC, one of the country&rsquo;s largest health systems, and Allegheny Health Network draw travel nurses and medical trainees, while Carnegie Mellon and the University of Pittsburgh bring students, researchers, and tech interns.</p><p>The city is built on hills and rivers, crossed by hundreds of bridges, with neighborhoods that each feel like small towns. Housing is mostly older brick homes and duplexes, along with newer apartment buildings in areas like Lawrenceville, the Strip District, and East Liberty. Downtown, known locally as the Golden Triangle, sits where the Allegheny and Monongahela rivers meet to form the Ohio, and many popular neighborhoods are a short bus ride east.</p><p>Pittsburgh is generally affordable compared with other Northeast cities. <strong>Ask about heating, hills, and parking</strong>: older homes vary in efficiency, some streets are steep, and parking can be tight in dense neighborhoods.</p>',
