    'prices' => '<p>Pittsburgh is among the more affordable large Northeast cities. Furnished private rooms commonly advertise somewhere in the $600&ndash;$1,000 per month range, while entire furnished one-bedrooms in popular neighborhoods typically run higher, often $1,300 or more.</p><p>These ranges are rough estimates, not official data. Prices vary by season, neighborhood and furnishing, so compare current listings before committing.</p>',
    'transit'=> '<p>Pittsburgh Regional Transit operates buses, dedicated busways, and the T light rail line, which runs from downtown to the South Hills. The East Busway connects downtown to the eastern neighborhoods, and the Monongahela and Duquesne inclines climb Mount Washington. Many residents drive, but Oakland, Shadyside, and Squirrel Hill are well served by buses.</p><p>Pittsburgh International Airport is west of the city, reachable by car or the 28X Airport Flyer bus.</p>',
